Rebased onto main `06992c92ad`; the new head `fd553e47cf` includes the required CI base `ddd4600197a4`. `git range-diff` confirms both fix patches are unchanged.

I reran the 88 CPU tests and 49 GPU tests (44 core + 5 issue regressions) on this head; all passed, with no skips. GPU validation used NVIDIA L20 / Qwen3-0.6B / Triton, with dependencies updated to match main. The PR description now contains the updated validation details. The earlier late-HTTP-error concern was also [verified as resolved](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/38850#discussion_r3985150090).

@Kangyan-Zhou could you enable CI with `/tag-and-rerun-ci` and help route the remaining review for this scripted-runtime test-harness fix? Thank you.

@Kangyan-Zhou following up on the CI and review request for this scripted-runtime test-harness fix. Could you please enable CI with `/tag-and-rerun-ci` and help route it to an appropriate reviewer?

The head is still `fd553e47cf`. Lint passed, and our validation on this head passed all 88 CPU and 49 L20 GPU tests. The earlier late-failure concern was [confirmed resolved](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/38850#discussion_r3985150090); upstream test jobs remain gated on `run-ci`.

Please let me know if a rebase or any additional validation would help move this forward. Thank you!

